{"agent_mode": null, "bash_calls": 3, "candidate_provenance": null, "cell_seed": 12941165400229337059, "checker_exit": 0, "checker_stderr": "", "checker_stdout": "round_money rounds half up; other helpers intact\nOBENCH_VERDICT: pass\n", "checker_workspace_files": {"pricing/__init__.py": {"bytes": 0, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"}, "pricing/money.py": {"bytes": 615, "mtime": 1791872315.3239408, "sha256": "85e3fbb51375eaaa484a2ef37839d7e6d1db0cb280e74cb6231ef4689ac7e589"}, "tests/test_round_money.py": {"bytes": 295, "mtime": 1791872318.2079258, "sha256": "49515ed204edcbf6c6f872e8cc919263bcca8bb9c5a4b47402afeb0fe5cdeb53"}, "tests/test_split.py": {"bytes": 101, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "f21bbe9cf15cf7f51ff9f71318aca4794c29f5d66cb9ae2aa0d4c919043d9bcf"}}, "child_edit_calls": 0, "child_plan_reminder": false, "cmd": ["/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/1b5c7b53d2c460b2ede60d78591b6826facf0e4d/omp", "-p", "`round_money(2.675)` returns `2.67` but customers expect `2.68`. Fix it.\n", "--mode", "json", "--provider", "vertex-anthropic", "--model", "claude-opus-5-5", "--yolo", "--session-dir", "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-38/omp-38/transcripts/with/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/21/session"], "completed": true, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 2, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-38/omp-38/cells/with/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/21/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/18.1.8 (/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/1b5c7b53d2c460b2ede60d78591b6826facf0e4d/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Next, a regression test covering the reported value, the banker's-rounding case (`0.125`), and a negative value:\nFixed: `round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`.\n\n**Cause:** the float `2.675` is actually stored as `2.67499999\u2026`, so the built-in `round(x, 2)` rounds it down. `round()` also rounds exact halves to the nearest even digit, so `round(0.125, 2)` gives `0.12`. The docstring promises half up. I confirmed the old behaviour: `2.67 0.12`.\n\n**Fix** in `pricing/money.py`: `round_money` now turns the float into its shortest decimal form (`str(2.675)` is `\"2.675\"`), rounds that half up to cents with `Decimal`, and still returns a float, so `add_vat` and any other caller works as before. Negative halves round away from zero (`-2.675` gives `-2.68`).\n\n**Test:** I added `tests/test_round_money.py`, covering `2.675`, `0.125`, `-2.675` and `2.674`. pytest isn't installed here, so I called the test functions directly with python3. The new test and the existing `test_split` both pass, and `add_vat(10)` still gives `12.0`.\n\n**Not changed \u2014 a separate risk in `split`:** it truncates with `int(total * 100)`. For amounts like `0.29`, `0.29 * 100` comes out as `28.999\u2026`, which truncates to `28`. The extra cent then gets added back to the first part, so the parts sum to the right total, but `base` is computed from the wrong value. Say if you want that fixed too.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 9, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 250349, "requests_cache_write": 11672, "requests_cost_usd": 0.1540298, "requests_count": 9, "requests_input_uncached": 20, "requests_output": 2276, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-bugfix-regress:claude-opus-5-5:trial21", "run_seed": 20261014, "sampling